iew_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T14:54:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T14:58:58Z","body":"Ok issue has been fixed for me atleast.. so i am closing it with the things i did to resolve it.. It was NOT Godot Bug. but my own dumb fault.. (mistake on my part sorry)\n\nMy Work Drive is on an NTFS drive that didn’t have proper Linux permissions when i mounted (my dumb mistake), so Godot (through gio) couldn’t create the Trash folder it needed.\n\nI fixed it by editing my `/etc/fstab` line for that drive and adding: `uid=1000,gid=1000,permissions`\n\n\nThen I remounted it and recreated the .Trash-1000 folder in the work drive\nAfter that, deleting files in Godot worked fine.\n\nThe way i found it is by Running godot via terminal, after deleting the file it gave these errors.\n\n`gio: file:///mnt/Work/Projects/Godot/Test/new%20folder: Unable to find or create trash directory /mnt/Work/.Trash-1000 to trash /mnt/Work/Projects/Godot/Test/new folder`\n`ERROR: Could not create child process: kioclient5 at: execute (drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp:936)`\n`ERROR: Could not create child process: gvfs-trash at: execute (drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp:936)`\n`amdgpu: The CS has been rejected, see dmesg for more information (-22).`\n\nand since i was using Arch and Hyprland both which comes barebones. had to mount the drives manually and this happened.. :D","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394609249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]